    // To make merging simple, we track whether u is incident to any selected child-edge.
    // Final local contribution at u depends on number of selected child edges k and t:
    // degree = k+t must be <=2.
    // Also, if t=0 and k>0, then all selected child-edges incident to u belong to the
    // same connected component through u, so k must be <=2 and if k>=1 they merge into
    // one component completed inside subtree(u).
